    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b2b36d35-fa88-5b51-b3e8-49528e7c2610" activityNameId="b3c5ecb0-605e-573d-a098-5f3b2e43e4c6" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">SOx retained, in lignite flue gas desulphurisation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: SOx retained, in lignite flue gas desulphurisation
The efficiency of the desulphurisation is 90 %. All environmental burdens associated with the operation of the scrubber are allocated to the SO2 retained and hence to the power plant. Therefore the produced gypsum is assumed to be burden free, and not explicitly included in the module.;
Synonyms: Wet scrubber, DeSOx, REA; 
UUID: 39e6804b-c087-3832-a18c-6a0bb17d4a9a
The module describes the operation of a wet scrubber. It includes material input, transport of this material and solid waste. The waste water is used for keeping wet the ash from power plant operation, which are disposed of in the power plant module.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Average installed technology in the 1990s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_39e6804b-c087-3832-a18c-6a0bb17d4a9a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
